You are building a web app for an elevator service company in the Philippines.

Tech stack: React 18 + Vite, JavaScript (no TypeScript), Tailwind CSS, Supabase (auth + database + storage), React Router v6, deployed on Vercel.

Design system:
- Gold: #D4AF37, Beige: #F5F5DC, Dark gray: #2C2C2C, Muted: #888888, Error red: #8B0000
- Fonts: Tahoma (body), Georgia (headings)
- No rounded corners, no shadows — flat bordered cards with gold border (#D4AF37)
- Buttons: gold background (#D4AF37) + dark text (#2C2C2C), or white with gold border

Key principles:
- Keep files under 200 lines when possible.
- All API calls go in src/lib/api.js using the Supabase client.
- Auth context is in src/contexts/AuthContext.jsx — use useAuth() hook for role/user.
- Roles: admin (Boss, full access), operations (field ops, limited access).
- Pages follow the pattern: List → Detail → Form (create/edit).
- Gate-based pipeline is the core UX — steps must be completed in sequence.

Domain terms: pipeline, step, gate, PIC (project-in-charge), subcon, T&C (testing & commissioning), handover, AMC (maintenance contract), breakdown call.

When making changes:
- Only modify files that actually need changes.
- Match the existing gold/beige design exactly — no new color schemes.
- Be concise. No unnecessary explanations unless asked.
- Output production-ready code that fits existing patterns.
